# DEVAI checkout normalization policy.
#
# RH-B records SHA256 identities for committed release inputs
# (requirements.in, lock/*.txt) and builds a deterministic release artifact from
# committed blobs. Those identities are only meaningful if a checkout produces
# the SAME BYTES on every platform.
#
# Without this file, GitHub's windows-* runner images (core.autocrlf=true)
# rewrite LF -> CRLF on checkout, so the identical commit yields different
# release-input SHA256 values on Windows than on Linux. STEP 6 observed exactly
# that: a default Windows checkout produced
#   requirements.in          6ba8f9b8... instead of 275bdf24...
#   lock/windows-cp313.txt   1b8f0285... instead of a2647d67...
#   lock/linux-cp313.txt     27912d49... instead of 05c9744b...
# and the release-input identity gate correctly failed closed.
#
# Force LF in the worktree for every text file so checkout is byte-stable
# across platforms and architectures.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.py   text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.in   text eol=lf
*.cfg  text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf

# Never rewrite binary content.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.tar  binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.pdb  binary
*.lib  binary
*.whl  binary
*.vhdx binary